# BBB Server Change Discipline (Git First)

Prefer git → remote repo → server update. Do **not** treat ad-hoc server file drops as the long-term delivery path.

## Required order (default)

1. Change code in this git repo locally.
2. Commit/push **only when the user asks**.
3. Update the BBB server from the approved flow (CI packages, or documented `deploy.sh` / pull).

## Forbidden without explicit user request

- Hot-patching **non-test** / production package trees as the primary fix
- Dropping jars beside packaged `bbb-web` / Akka / GraphQL artifacts
- Hand-editing `/usr/share/bbb-web`, recording pipelines, or mediasoup as delivery

## Allowed — live51 HTML5 hot-fix (SafeMeet test)

**live51** (host from gitignored `.deploy.env`, typically `live51.roomeet.ir` / `78.157.39.51`) is the SafeMeet **test** BBB for UI iteration.

When the user wants quick feedback and full CI would be wasteful:

- Use skill [hotfix-live51-html5](.cursor/skills/hotfix-live51-html5/SKILL.md)
- Scope: `bigbluebutton-html5` client assets (JS/TS/CSS/skyroom) only
- CSS-only → rsync stylesheets to live html5-client; JS → remote `npm run build` + sync `dist/`
- Do **not** commit/push unless asked; user batches to git + CI/CD later

Still allowed anytime: read-only SSH inspection; documented `./deploy.sh --only html5` when requested.

If an out-of-band hot-fix was applied, remind the user it is not on the remote repository until they push.
